-- #1300 DRAIN: `import m.{Ctor(..)}` where `Ctor` names a CONSTRUCTOR, not a type.
--
-- `(..)` is a SUFFIX on an import member, not a separate syntactic form, so it is
-- legal after any member — including one that names a constructor, where it simply
-- has nothing to expand.  `backend/private_mangle.ctorMemberEntry` read it as a
-- separate form: its wild branch looked `Jjw` up in a TYPE-keyed table, missed, and
-- returned `[]`, so `Jjw` never entered the unit's constructor-rename map while
-- qmodw's definition was renamed `qmodw__Jjw` as usual.
--
-- Expected output, derived by hand BEFORE any capture and independently of any
-- engine: `Jjw` can only mean qmodw's `Jjw : Int -> QTW`, so `unQW (Jjw 5)` = `5`;
-- `Kkw` is pmodw's arity-2 one, so `unPW (Kkw 1 2)` = `1 + 2` = `3`.  So `5` then `3`.
--
-- ⚠️ COUNTERFACTUAL, measured rather than asserted.  With
-- `compiler/backend/private_mangle.mdk` restored to bfee53b4 and the binary rebuilt,
-- this fixture is RED on the native arm:
--     $ medaka build entry.mdk -o e
--     error: emitter failed compiling entry.mdk
--     runtime error [E-PANIC]: unbound variable 'Jjw' (not a local, ctor, or known fn)
--     exit 1
-- while `medaka run entry.mdk` prints `5` / `3` at exit 0.  So only an arm that
-- GRADES THE BUILD can see this — which is why the fixture lives in a corpus
-- `diff_compiler_engines.sh` reads.
--
-- ⚠️ THE SECOND ASSERTION IS THE BYSTANDER, and it is about the OPPOSITE direction.
-- The cheap way to make a `(..)` member on a ctor bind something is to hand it every
-- constructor of the named member's OWNING type.  That would put qmodw's NULLARY
-- `Kkw` into the rename map, and the map is first-entry-wins over decls in source
-- order (`omFromPairs (reverseL rmList)`, private_mangle.mdk), with qmodw's clause
-- first — so `Kkw 1 2` would bind the nullary constructor instead of pmodw's arity-2
-- one.  The clause ORDER is the trigger and must not be "tidied": qmodw must stay
-- first.  The shipped fix does NOT expand at all on this path (it binds `Jjw` alone,
-- mirroring `frontend/resolve.expandMemberNames`), so this half is green both before
-- and after — it guards the next edit, not this one.
import qmodw.{Jjw(..), unQW}
import pmodw.{PW, Kkw, unPW}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  let _ = putStrLn (intToString (unQW (Jjw 5)))
  putStrLn (intToString (unPW (Kkw 1 2)))
